spec ww02-stale-snapshot-write: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# WW02. s2 takes its snapshot at BEGIN; s1 writes the same node and commits after it.
# s2's write must be refused whenever s1's version is in flight or committed after
# s2's snapshot (first-updater-wins / first-committer-wins, F2). PostgreSQL READ
# COMMITTED would re-fetch and succeed; snapshot isolation cannot.

starting permutation: s1w s1c s2w s2c
step s1w: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.v = 1 RETURN n.v AS v
v
-
1
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2w: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.v = 2 RETURN n.v AS v
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: COMMIT
ERROR: cypher: transaction poisoned by a prior failed Exec statement — call Rollback
final final: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) RETURN n.v AS v
v
-
1
(1 row)

